firewalld service for a Ghost host, at ghostd.toml's defaults: the lobby
([lobby] port) and one port per session ([sessions] port_base and max).
A host with other ports copies this to /etc/firewalld/services and edits
it there. Installing it opens nothing: add the service "ghostd" to a zone.
-->
<service>
  <short>Ghost host</short>
  <description>Ghost remote desktop host: ghostd's lobby, which spectre connects to first, and one UDP port per running session.</description>
  <port protocol="udp" port="4442"/>
  <port protocol="udp" port="14400-14463"/>
</service>
